  "trainingNote": "Prologue display XP per completed foraging/plant-harvest action; focus applies. Empty completed attempts train too. Training stops at Survival 3. These rates use the local skill scale, not raw CDDA XP.",
  "bashRules": {
    "//": "Breaking a thing up for what it is made of. Only once it has been picked over, so nothing is lost; whichever of dismantling and bashing is done first takes the thing with it. The pace comes from what is swung: heavier is faster, and a purpose-made hammer helps. Bare hands will not do it.",
    "minBashDamage": 6,
    "hammerLevel": 2,
    "hammerFactor": 0.85,
    "fallback": {
      "//": "27.09.2026: anything that can be taken apart can also be bashed apart, for a rough share of the same parts. Each part of the dismantling comes out with `prob`, at `share` of its count (at least one); the time is `minutesFactor` of the dismantling's, then paced by the tool as above.",
      "prob": 0.7,
      "share": [0.25, 0.6],
      "minutesFactor": 0.6
    },
    "staminaPerMinute": 1,
    "tiers": [
      {
        "bash": 18,
        "factor": 0.55
      },
      {
        "bash": 10,
        "factor": 0.8
      }
    ],
    "//tiers": "Crush damage of the best thing within reach: a crowbar or a sledge is quickest, a pipe or a plank middling, a rock the slowest that works at all. The listed minutes are the time with a rock.",
    "//gives": "`charges` for anything the world counts by charges (scrap, nails, wire); `count` for whole pieces."
  },
